KG42.register("source_edge_archive-be19690cfb7ddaac895cec35",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","target":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","source_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","target_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::bidding.demand","target_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. | Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. | Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. | Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Termination of iterative RCI coordination.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"b00508466f6b2022a84dfbc98b1373b0a6a1ce4dc14c11418a2966deecf6fdbd","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"M01","source_definition":"The perceived bilateral price supplies an input to the target requested-power setpoint calculation. Scope: Target-setpoint calculation for the consumer branch of decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: The negotiating agent acts as a consumer. Updating bilateral trading-price estimates precedes updating requested-energy decision variables within each RCI iteration. Scope: Sequence of updates within an RCI iteration, restricted to the requested-energy decision variables of consumers. Different offered prices direct the consumer to try to request as much as possible from the neighbor with the most favorable price and nothing from the others. Scope: The discussed direct-solution alternative for consumer local MBED subproblems, rather than the implemented RCI gradient update. Condition: A consumer directly solves its local subproblem when offered different prices. Requested bilateral quantities are nonpositive under the injection convention. RCI enforces this sign restriction at every iteration using the consumer min projection. Scope: Consumer requested-energy quantities in MBED and their iterative RCI updates. Condition: The agent acts as a consumer. The aggregate requested quantity, represented as the consumer's net power injection, is constrained by the agent's lower and upper power boundaries. Scope: Feasibility of consumer requested quantities in MBED. Condition: The agent acts as a consumer; the restriction concerns feasible power setpoints. The current requested bilateral quantity must be included in the information sent to the neighboring agent. Scope: Communication of consumer quantity estimates during decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each iteration, for a consumer and its neighboring negotiating agent.","target_definition":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity.","expression":"λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11), for a consumer n ∈ Ω_c with P_nm^k ≤ 0 (9e) and m ∈ ω_n; the term (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) is the trading-reciprocity imbalance (innovation) term that carries the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity into the price-estimate update.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-P-nm","x-P-mn","x-lambda-nm","x-lambda-mn"],"parameter_refs":["theta-alpha-k","theta-beta-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e07"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"m- The power set-points of an agent n are constrained by the ny power boundaries Pn and Pn, ms a Pn ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The role of each agent is restrained to either producer or consumer (P_n P̄_n ≥ 0) as it simplifies the following derivations. Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 34, NO. 2, MARCH 2019 equality constraint (as in the dual a","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"This is referred to as the λ-update, λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11) where α^k and β^k are sequences of positive factors such that any excitation is persistent, so that the series of each sequence diverges [12]. The tuning of these parameters is key to the performance of the algorithm and will usually be a trade-off between convergence speed and resilience to change of setup. The tuning relies as much on the value of the parameters as on the ratio between the two. The performance could be improved by using adaptive factors that adjust this ratio."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-D. Operational Aspects of the Iterative Process","anchor_text":"privacy and support data security since very little information is shared and only with those agents","equation_id":"(23)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Here to perform the RCI updates, a minimum set of informa-tion is to be shared. As such, at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk  of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following:\n             F nmk = {P nm,k   λknm}                (23)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 34, NO. 2, MARCH 2019 equality constraint (as in the dual a","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"where αk and βk are sequences of positive factors such that any excitation is persistent, so that the series of each sequence diverges [12]. The tuning of these parameters is key to the performance of the algorithm and will usually be a trade-off between convergence speed and resilience to change of setup. The tuning relies as much on the value of the parameters as on the ratio between the two. The performance could be improved by using adaptive factors that adjust this ratio."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. | Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. | Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. | Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Termination of iterative RCI coordination.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"paper_scope_note":"The λ update, P update, and required communication of RCI have direct formula basis; only protocol component dependencies are allowed, and the values of k and k+1 or the roles of consumer and producer are not conflated."}});
